#title()
We will introduce version control, Git, and GitHub.
It will be a very hands-on session, so make sure to bring a laptop with Git set up.
A guide will be made available and distributed beforehand for those uncertain on how to set up Git.
There will be a short morning session for anyone who wants help setting up their system, followed by an afternoon session where we get into Git.
We will cover all the essentials, from pushing and pulling, to setting up remotes and collaborating.
This will be accompanied by exercises, activities, and challenges.
We will also look at some GitHub specific features, time permitting.
Notes, slides, and follow-up reading will be provided.
